RESOLUTION - Endorsing a study of the costs of new development for future policy
decisions regarding relative public and private responsibilities for capital investments
necessitated by development – referred to Finance Committee (sponsors – Dr. Rinne and Mayor
Kaysen).  Mr. Brown advised the item was discussed under other items for the agenda at the
August 19 Finance Committee meeting, and provisions of Title 2 of City Code had been met.
th
Mr. Brown moved to adopt, seconded by Ms. Broyles.  Matt Ashby, Planning Services Director,
noted the study concept had been associated with provisions attached to a recent development
action and that members of the governing body had expressed that the study would be more
appropriately addressed independently rather than attaching it to one specific development
project.  He noted the resolution will involve issuance of a request for proposals (RFP) to select
a consultant to provide information related to community growth issues.  Questions were raised
on the possibility of forming a committee to assist in overseeing the study’s progress, study
funding source, and whether a provision could be contained in the contract for services to provide
for a timely reporting process that includes City Council members.  In response, Mr. Ashby
advised this type of study generally could involve a steering committee to help guide the project
and that the Council and executive administration could determine committee composition.
Upon inquiry, Lois Huff, City Treasurer, advised once there was a contract or RFP done to
determine the amount needed, options for funding the study could be presented.  Further
comment followed on purpose of the study and support for study components to be “all
inclusive” relative to all areas involving development costs, including the Board of Public
